+# check-change round 1, Layer 2 -- category: harness -- PR #832
+# Grounded only in plan/788/base committed sources. Severity per rules/pr.md.
+category: harness
+base: plan/788/base
+principles:
+  - {id: H1, source: "plan/788/base:CLAUDE.md 'Play Pipeline Rules'", principle: "Anything touching the agent/skill flow or what a play decides is an intent change: edit reference/ice.md, recompile with /edit-play. Direct SKILL.md edits are for output format and wiring only."}
+  - {id: H2, source: "plan/788/base:CLAUDE.md 'Agents hold the role of Context Crafting' and .claude/rules/garura-memory.md", principle: "Agents gather context and put it on files; memory is read only through the memory tool by agents."}
+  - {id: H3, source: "plan/788/base:docs/adr/031-business-intent-and-ice.md Affects line", principle: "Every copy of lint_grounding.py is changed together; copies must not drift."}
+  - {id: H4, source: "plan/788/base:CLAUDE.md 'Play Pipeline Rules' durability rule + docs/adr/039", principle: "Shared scaffolding lives once and is pointed to; a new check must not leave the repo failing its own linter."}
+findings:
+  - {category: harness, id: HA1, severity: P2, path: core/components/plays/edit-ontology/SKILL.md, basis: "H1", message: "Step 1 now has product-os-keeper load asking-a-person.md via the memory tool, write it to <working>/asking-a-person.md, and pass it as new contract input asking_rule to Steps 1, 3 and 5. That is a change to the agent/skill flow and contract, not wording. reference/ice.md was not touched and does not mention the rule, so the next /edit-play rebuild will drop it. Either update ice.md and recompile, or record why this is wiring only.", status: open}
+  - {category: harness, id: HA2, severity: P3, path: core/components/plays/edit-ontology/SKILL.md, basis: "H2", message: "Direction is consistent with H2 (agent loads rule through the memory tool, skill reads only the file the agent put in STM). No violation; the product-os-keeper agent definition itself was not updated to list this duty.", status: open}
+  - {category: harness, id: HB1, severity: P2, path: core/tools/lint-components/lib/rules/asking-a-person.js, basis: "H4", message: "On real plays the rule adds 30 errors (lint-components 121 to 151). Only edit-ontology is fixed in this PR; 29 plays/loops now fail the linter. The PR body states the fix is #831, so the merge lands a red linter on the plan branch. Accepted-as-deferred only if #831 lands before the plan merges to main.", status: "deferred: #831"}
+  - {category: harness, id: HB2, severity: P3, path: core/tools/lint-components/lib/rules/asking-a-person.js, basis: "H4", message: "False positives: signals match any line, including front-matter descriptions and prose mentions. Seen on real files: release-epic line 4 (description text), shape-quality-lens line 48 (mentions 'a typed approval' in a constraint), create-play line 121 ('interview and asks for approval' in a note about itself). Detection has no scoping to checkpoint steps. Also the content.includes('asking-a-person.md') pointer test accepts a mention anywhere, so a stray mention passes (false negative).", status: open}
+  - {category: harness, id: HB3, severity: P4, path: core/tools/lint-components/lib/rules/asking-a-person.js, basis: "H4", message: "False negatives: a play that asks through phrasing not in the six patterns (for example 'wait for the reply', 'Tether/Vanish' alone, 'confirm with the person') is not caught. Acceptable for a first rule; note the list is a heuristic.", status: open}
+  - {category: harness, id: HC1, severity: P2, path: "core/components/plays/*/scripts/lint_grounding.py", basis: "H3", message: "All 12 copies are byte-identical (same md5), as required. But there is no canonical source create-play stamps from, and no check that the copies match; the only rule is the ADR 031 line 'every copy'. Identity depends on whoever edits next touching all 12. Recommend a canonical file plus an identity check (check-components).", status: open}
+  - {category: harness, id: HC2, severity: P4, path: core/components/plays/discover-domains/scripts/test_lint_slice_intents.py, basis: "H3", message: "New slice-intents behaviour is tested in one play's folder only; fine since copies are identical, but the test does not cover the other 11 copies.", status: open}
+  - {category: harness, id: HD1, severity: P3, path: core/components/skills/author-product-ontology/SKILL.md, basis: "H2", message: "asking_rule is marked required for scope, kinds, links. No other caller of this skill is shown to pass it; if another play invokes the skill it now has a missing required input.", status: open}
